{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_0148bbHoK3rTBNhwzVYBYdzo","type":"tool_result","content":"## Assignment for approval: discourse (job 0def57ff)\n\nRecommended architecture: Aurora PostgreSQL and DynamoDB\n\nThe analysis covered 311 tables and 1654 query patterns across two candidate engines, Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL and Amazon DynamoDB. Both engines stay: Aurora PostgreSQL serves the 937 queries that need joins, aggregations and transactional writes, and DynamoDB serves the 717 queries built on key lookups and key-range reads. Changes committed to Aurora PostgreSQL reach DynamoDB through change data capture, so each engine holds the data in the shape its queries need.\n\n| Engine | Queries before | Queries final | Share of final | Outcome |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\n| Aurora PostgreSQL | 937 | 937 | 56.7% | kept |\n| DynamoDB | 717 | 717 | 43.3% | kept |\n\nTotal: 1654 queries.\n\nEngines in scope: Aurora PostgreSQL, DynamoDB (customer's choice).\n\nReality check changed nothing: the assignment stays as routed.\n\nArchitectural patterns:\n- Event-Driven Sync\n  - When: Multiple engines need the same data in different shapes\n  - Change data capture on Aurora PostgreSQL carries each committed change to DynamoDB. Each consumer shapes the data for its own access patterns.\n\nSchema design runs next for: Aurora PostgreSQL, DynamoDB.\n\n- Summary page (the query flow and every query's engine): http://localhost:3000/analysis/monitor/summary/0def57ff","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4967eb72-5c65-41db-98a2-fcb5ea54b80f","uuid":"fb7b0e3e-f815-43dc-85af-1c5ae727d725","timestamp":"2026-10-27T16:18:35.388Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## Assignment for approval: discourse (job 0def57ff)\n\nRecommended architecture: Aurora PostgreSQL and DynamoDB\n\nThe analysis covered 311 tables and 1654 query patterns across two candidate engines, Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL and Amazon DynamoDB. Both engines stay: Aurora PostgreSQL serves the 937 queries that need joins, aggregations and transactional writes, and DynamoDB serves the 717 queries buil\n[... 553 characters trimmed ...]\nt-Driven Sync\n  - When: Multiple engines need the same data in different shapes\n  - Change data capture on Aurora PostgreSQL carries each committed change to DynamoDB. Each consumer shapes the data for its own access patterns.\n\nSchema design runs next for: Aurora PostgreSQL, DynamoDB.\n\n- Summary page (the query flow and every query's engine): http://localhost:3000/analysis/monitor/summary/0def57ff","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
